    { t: "mcq", q: "Under pressure, even top athletes can ____ why they started the sport in the first place.", o: ["single out", "check in on", "liaise with", "lose sight of"], a: 3, k: "vocab", x: "lose sight of = يغفل عن الهدف الأساسي. أما single out فتعني «يختار من بين الآخرين»، وcheck in on «يطمئن على»، وliaise with «ينسّق مع»." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "The coach's remarks were meant to encourage the squad, but they had the opposite effect. Singled out in front of everyone, the goalkeeper felt humiliated, and his confidence, already fragile, collapsed. By the end of the week the speech had backfired on the coach: several players had stopped listening to him altogether.\n\nIn the text, 'backfired on' is closest in meaning to …", o: ["produced the opposite result for", "was loudly applauded by", "was carefully planned by", "was quickly forgotten by"], a: 0, k: "vocab", x: "الجملة تقول إن الكلمات «had the opposite effect» وإن اللاعبين توقفوا عن الاستماع، فـ backfire on = جاءت نتيجتها عكسية وضارّة بصاحبها." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "The museum is free on Fridays, so you ____ buy a ticket.", o: ["mustn't", "needn't to", "don't have to", "ought not"], a: 2, k: "g12u5-gr1", x: "المتحف مجاني فشراء التذكرة غير ضروري ← don't have to. أما mustn't فتعني «ممنوع»، وneedn't لا يأتي بعدها to، وought not تحتاج إلى to." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "We lost the match because we didn't practise penalties. We ____ practised them more.", o: ["must have", "should have", "can't have", "needn't have"], a: 1, k: "g12u5-gr1", x: "لوم أو ندم على شيء لم نفعله ← should have + V3. أما must have وcan't have فللاستنتاج، وneedn't have تعني «لم يكن ضرورياً»." },
    { t: "err", q: "She mustn't have seen the sign, otherwise she would have stopped.", w: "mustn't", c: "can't", k: "g12u5-gr2", x: "الجملة الثانية تدل على أننا متأكدون أنها لم ترَ اللافتة، والاستنتاج السلبي القوي عن الماضي يكون بـ can't have + V3 وليس mustn't have." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "____ you apply yourself, you will not pass the driving test.", o: ["Providing", "In case", "As long as", "Unless"], a: 3, k: "g12u5-gr3", x: "Unless = if … not، فالمعنى: ما لم تجتهد لن تنجح. أما Providing وAs long as فتعنيان «بشرط أن» وتعطيان معنى معاكساً، وIn case تعني «تحسّباً لـ»." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence means the same as: 'It wasn't necessary for her to take a taxi, but she did.'?", o: ["She needn't have taken a taxi.", "She mustn't have taken a taxi.", "She couldn't have taken a taxi.", "She shouldn't take a taxi."], a: 0, k: "g12u5-gr1", x: "فعلت شيئاً لم يكن ضرورياً ← needn't have + V3. أما couldn't have فتعني «مستحيل أن تكون…»، وmustn't have لا تؤدي هذا المعنى، وshouldn't take صيغة حاضرة." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence means the same as: 'It's possible that the goalkeeper didn't hear the whistle.'?", o: ["The goalkeeper can't have heard the whistle.", "The goalkeeper might not have heard the whistle.", "The goalkeeper mustn't have heard the whistle.", "The goalkeeper needn't have heard the whistle."], a: 1, k: "g12u5-gr2", x: "possible that … didn't ← might not have + V3 (ربما لم يسمع). أما can't have فتعني «متأكد أنه لم يسمع»، وneedn't have تعني «لم يكن ضرورياً أن يسمع»." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence means the same as: 'Because he did not know the way, Yazan asked a passer-by.'?", o: ["Knowing not the way, Yazan asked a passer-by.", "Not known the way, Yazan asked a passer-by.", "Not knowing the way, Yazan asked a passer-by.", "Not to know the way, Yazan asked a passer-by."], a: 2, k: "g12u5-gr3", x: "السبب بصيغة النفي ← Not knowing (Not + V-ing). صيغة Knowing not قديمة وغير مستعملة، وNot known مبني للمجهول فيغيّر المعنى، وNot to know تدل على الغرض." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence means the same as: 'I regret not asking for help earlier.'?", o: ["I wish I asked for help earlier.", "I wish I had asked for help earlier.", "I wish I would ask for help earlier.", "I wish I have asked for help earlier."], a: 1, k: "g12u5-gr3", x: "الندم على الماضي يُعبَّر عنه بـ wish + past perfect: I wish I had asked." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "You have reached the Test Centre results line. Candidates who took this morning's theory test needn't call again: results will be posted online after four o'clock. Those who did not pass are allowed to rebook at once, but learners are not permitted to drive unaccompanied until they have passed.\n\nWhat can we conclude from the message?", o: ["Everyone who took the test has passed.", "Failed candidates must wait until the evening to rebook.", "Candidates can see their results online, so phoning is unnecessary.", "Learners may drive alone while they wait for their results."], a: 2, k: "reading", x: "needn't call again + results will be posted online ← لا حاجة للاتصال لأن النتائج ستظهر على الإنترنت. أما الراسبون فمسموح لهم بإعادة الحجز فوراً (are allowed to rebook at once)، والمتدربون غير مسموح لهم بالقيادة دون مرافق (not permitted to drive unaccompanied)." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Some students believe that staying up all night before an exam is a sign of dedication. In my view, it is nothing of the kind. Having ignored the subject for weeks, they try to cram it into a few frantic hours, and the result is usually a mind running on empty. Surely a little effort every day would be wiser?\n\nThe writer's attitude to all-night revision is …", o: ["admiring", "critical", "indifferent", "uncertain"], a: 1, k: "reading", x: "عبارات الكاتب In my view, it is nothing of the kind وfrantic وSurely a little effort every day would be wiser? تدل على موقف ناقد من السهر قبل الامتحان." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Before the sun has rubbed the sleep from its eyes,\nI lace my shoes and meet the empty road.\nIt asks for nothing but one more step,\nthen one more after that.\nBy the time the city wakes, I have already won\nthe only race that matters: the one with yesterday.\n\nWhat is the poem's main message?", o: ["Real success means doing better than your own earlier self, one step at a time.", "The best time to train is before sunrise.", "Runners should never compete against other people.", "Cities should wake up earlier."], a: 0, k: "reading", x: "السطر الأخير يقول إن السباق الوحيد المهم هو «السباق مع الأمس»، أي أن النجاح أن تتفوّق على نفسك السابقة خطوة بعد خطوة (one more step…)." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "A forum user writes: 'I always run out of steam by nine p.m. Any tips?' Which reply is the most helpful and polite?", o: ["Stop being lazy and get your head down.", "That is not my problem.", "You must follow my plan exactly or you will fail.", "Have you thought about studying in short bursts? That works for me."], a: 3, k: "speaking", x: "الرد المهذب المفيد يقترح بصيغة سؤال (Have you thought about…?) ويشارك تجربة شخصية (That works for me). أما الردود الأخرى فجارحة أو غير مفيدة أو آمرة." },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence would NOT be appropriate in a formal opinion essay?", o: ["It must be admitted that memorisation has some value.", "Having weighed both views, I believe critical thinking matters more.", "Honestly, exams are such a pain, aren't they?", "Nevertheless, this approach has serious limitations."], a: 2, k: "writing", x: "المقالة الرسمية تتجنب العبارات العامية (Honestly, such a pain) والأسئلة الذيلية (aren't they?). أما الجمل الأخرى فرسمية: It must be admitted that…، Having weighed…، Nevertheless…" },
    { t: "mcq", q: "Which sentence uses hedging most appropriately in an academic essay?", o: ["Memorisation may be less useful than critical thinking in the long term.", "Memorisation is completely useless.", "Everybody knows that critical thinking is better.", "Critical thinking will definitely solve every problem."], a: 0, k: "writing", x: "التحوّط (hedging) يخفف الادعاء بكلمات مثل may / might / tends to / in the long term فلا يبدو الكاتب مبالغاً. أما بقية الجمل فقاطعة ومبالغ فيها (completely, Everybody knows, definitely every)." }
